title: A Faction Breaks Away
subtitle: A faction's quarrel with the party ends in a split.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: split_pending = 1 and rf_over = 0
on-arrival: {!
var f = Q.split_faction;
Q.split_name = window.RF.names[f];
Q.split_pending = 0;
window.RF.expel(Q, f);
!}

= The <span class="f-[+ split_faction +]">[+ split_name +]</span> leaves the party

The leadership has had enough, and so has the <span class="f-[+ split_faction +]">[+ split_name +]</span>. Its leaders are expelled for factional activity, and a share of the membership follows them out. They will form a small group of their own, as the <span class="p-kapd">KAPD</span> did in 1920 and as the KPO and the Leninbund would later.
